# verbs.pdl - the deskopoly manifest: the known mechanics as data (pass 1, 2026-11-07; BOOK 08-roadmap/design-docs/HANDOFF-NOV-7 section 10, D48 BRAIN rows, D49 one door).
#   GAME / VERB rows keep the shape verbgen reads (events-hq ops/verbgen.c parses ONLY these two row types; I read its source, I did not run it on this file).
#   FLOW  | verb | reads | writes          which hard-state files a verb touches (read by `deskopoly mechanics`, so a viewer can draw the data flow without reading C)
#   BRAIN | dec_key | verb | phases | ok_outcomes | bad_outcomes | note     which verbs a pet may CHOOSE and which harness CASE names judge them (checked by brain_lint)
#   page: no for all of these in pass 1 (no event pages generated yet; S3 of the plan fires them through pages).
GAME | deskopoly | deskopoly_verb | ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | ops/deskopoly.c
VERB | new       | no | ui | seed players | start a game: writes the first ledger row (the seed is hard state)
VERB | lobby     | no | ui | ruleset | schema 2: open a classic game (first ledger row: ruleset name, rules hash, max players); players are NOT config, they join
VERB | join      | no | ui | name driver personality token | add a player in the lobby (next free id p1..p8, a free token 0..7); the roster is a ledger fact
VERB | leave     | no | ui | player id | remove a player from the lobby (before start)
VERB | start     | no | ui | seed | close the lobby (2..8 players) and record the seed and the rules hash
VERB | order     | no | ui | - | the next player throws for the opening order; the highest total moves first (ties re-throw); the call appends `first` when decided
VERB | bankrupt  | no | ui | as=pN | classic: the current player declares bankruptcy while a debt cannot be paid; all assets go to the creditor (a player) or back to the bank
VERB | jail_pay  | no | ui | as=pN | classic: pay the 50 fine to leave Jail, then roll normally
VERB | jail_card | no | ui | as=pN | classic: use a Get Out of Jail card (cards arrive in M5; refused until then)
VERB | jail_roll | no | ui | as=pN | classic: throw for doubles in Jail; doubles free you and you move that total (no extra roll); the third failed turn forces the 50 fine
VERB | build     | no | ui | tile as=pN | classic: build one house (or the hotel) on a street of a colour you own whole, evenly, from the 32 house / 12 hotel supply
VERB | sell      | no | ui | tile as=pN | classic: sell one building back for half its cost, evenly (also while in debt)
VERB | mortgage  | no | ui | tile as=pN | classic: mortgage a tile with no buildings in its colour for half its price (also while in debt)
VERB | unmortgage| no | ui | tile as=pN | classic: lift a mortgage for its value plus 10 percent, rounded up
VERB | pay_debt  | no | ui | as=pN | classic: pay the debt once the cash covers it (after selling or mortgaging)
VERB | help      | no | ui | verb | list the verbs (from this file) and, in a classic game, the phase and what is legal now
VERB | roll      | no | ui | as=pN        | the current player rolls two dice (seeded, recorded), moves, and the landing resolves (Start bonus, levy, rent, or a tile for sale)
VERB | buy       | no | ui | -            | buy the tile the current player stands on (refused when unaffordable or not for sale)
VERB | skip      | no | ui | -            | decline the tile for sale; in a classic game (auctions on, the default) the tile goes to AUCTION, left of you first, you last
VERB | bid       | no | ui | amount as=pN | classic auction: bid at least the minimum, then the standing bid plus the step, at most your cash; only the bidder whose turn it is; the call that ends the auction also records the bank auction_end row
VERB | pass      | no | ui | as=pN        | classic auction: drop out of this auction for good; when only the high bidder is left (or everyone passed) the auction ends: sold-to=<id>-<amount> or unsold
VERB | offer     | no | ui | pN give A get B | open a trade offer to pN (current player; PRE, POST or your DEBT; never BUY or AUCTION): assets are prop:<tile>+cash:<n>+card:<luck|fund>; one open offer per proposer, trade_offers_per_turn new offers per turn (default 3, 0 = off); NEVER blocks play
VERB | counter   | no | ui | id give A get B | the addressee answers with a NEW offer back (round + 1, at most trade_max_rounds); does not count against the allowance
VERB | amend     | no | ui | id give A get B | the proposer changes the terms of its own open offer (round unchanged, no allowance used)
VERB | accept    | no | ui | [id] as=pN | the addressee accepts: re-validated, then ONE atomic swap; the receiver of a mortgaged tile pays the bank 10% of its mortgage value; waits while an auction is open
VERB | reject    | no | ui | [id] as=pN | the addressee refuses the offer
VERB | cancel    | no | ui | [id] as=pN | the proposer withdraws its open offer
VERB | end_turn  | no | ui | -            | finish the turn; the next active player is up
VERB | autoplay  | no | ui | -            | play the whole game with each player's style (pets stand-in); writes decision rows
VERB | status    | no | ui | -            | read-only: the whole state, derived by replaying the ledger
VERB | replay    | no | ui | -            | read-only: replay the ledger and print its state hash (refuses a ledger that does not reproduce itself)
VERB | check     | no | ui | -            | read-only: replay plus invariants (money conservation, ownership, positions)
VERB | mechanics | no | ui | -            | read-only: the known mechanics and hard state as plain rows (a projection of these files, for an editor)
VERB | seat      | no | ui | player human\|pet | change who drives a seat (a ledger row, legal out of turn: a control change, not a game move)
VERB | audit     | no | ui | -            | read-only no-ghost-data check: state/ holds only the files state.pdl declares (LEDGER, PROJECTION, CONFIG, PREFERENCE); a projection must name a real regenerating verb
VERB | tick      | no | ui | -            | ONE step for the current seat: a pet seat performs its next verb, a human seat makes tick wait
VERB | ui        | no | ui | -            | write state/ui.txt: the window feed, a projection of the replayed ledger (show_* keys are 1 or EMPTY)
VERB | ledger_hash | no | ui | skip_verb  | read-only digest of the ledger rows, optionally without one verb (for example seat), so two games can be compared exactly
VERB | page      | no | ui | desk_dir atlas | draw the board as an editor desk page (cells.txt, map.txt, ...) from board.pdl + page.pdl + the replayed ledger; owned tiles show their owner
VERB | preview   | no | ui | desk_dir out.raw | a FLAT top-down picture of a desk (no depth, not the engine render), raw RGBA for raw_to_png
FLOW | new       | rules.pdl,board.pdl        | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | lobby     | rulesets/<name>/board.pdl,rules.pdl | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | join      | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | leave     | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | start     | state/ledger.txt,rulesets/<name>/rules.pdl | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | order     | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | bankrupt  | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | jail_pay  | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | jail_card | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | jail_roll | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | build     | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | sell      | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | mortgage  | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | unmortgage| state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | pay_debt  | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | help      | verbs.pdl,state/ledger.txt | -
FLOW | roll      | state/ledger.txt,board.pdl | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | buy       | state/ledger.txt,board.pdl | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | skip      | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | bid       | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | pass      | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | offer     | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | counter   | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | amend     | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | accept    | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | reject    | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | cancel    | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | end_turn  | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | autoplay  | state/ledger.txt,rules.pdl | state/ledger.txt,state/decisions.txt
FLOW | status    | state/ledger.txt           | -
FLOW | replay    | state/ledger.txt           | -
FLOW | check     | state/ledger.txt           | -
FLOW | mechanics | verbs.pdl,rules.pdl,board.pdl,state/ledger.txt | state/mechanics.txt
FLOW | seat      | state/ledger.txt           | state/ledger.txt
FLOW | audit     | state.pdl,verbs.pdl,state/ | -
FLOW | tick      | state/ledger.txt,rules.pdl | state/ledger.txt,state/decisions.txt
FLOW | ui        | state/ledger.txt           | state/ui.txt
FLOW | ledger_hash | state/ledger.txt        | -
FLOW | page      | board.pdl,page.pdl,state/ledger.txt | <desk_dir>/cells.txt,map.txt,events.txt,skin.txt,extrusion.pdl,cells.rgba
FLOW | preview   | <desk_dir>/cells.txt,cells.rgba | <out.raw>
BRAIN | roll     | roll     | rules,autoplay,refusals | ok  |                 | every turn starts with a roll; nothing to choose
BRAIN | buy      | buy      | autoplay,refusals       | ok  | blocked,refused | choose to buy the tile under you; blocked when the cash is not there
BRAIN | skip     | skip     | autoplay                | ok  |                 | choose to leave the tile for the bank
BRAIN | bid      | bid      | autoplay,refusals       | ok  | blocked,refused | bid the minimum raise while the price x style value and the cash allow (STOPGAP until M10); refused when below the minimum, below the standing bid plus the step, or above cash
BRAIN | pass     | pass     | autoplay                | ok  |                 | leave the auction when the next bid is beyond value or cash
BRAIN | offer    | offer    | autoplay,refusals       | ok  | blocked,refused | a pet PROPOSES a trade when RULE pet_trades is on (default off): the colour it would complete or come within one tile of, offered 1.5 x the tile price rounded to 10, only if it keeps 200 cash, one proposal per turn (STOPGAP until M10; judged in harness case dsk_pettrade); blocked by the per-turn allowance
BRAIN | accept   | accept   | autoplay,refusals       | ok  | blocked,refused | a pet accepts an offer addressed to it when the swap gains value (STOPGAP price x3-on-a-full-colour rule, M10 replaces it); refused when stale
BRAIN | reject   | reject   | autoplay                | ok  |                 | a pet refuses an offer that loses value
BRAIN | end_turn | end_turn | autoplay                | ok  |                 | hand the dice on
